  "visualBrief": "The Strasbourg and Verdun pavilions frame paired limestone gables, glazed fanlights, clocks and seated city figures. Their open arcades sit beneath the south marquise. A transverse concourse links the fourteen separately roofed platforms while the track gaps remain open.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 52 m sea-level datum follows standard viewer terrain. The pavilion foundations reach the sampled forecourt, the stairs meet the two entrance landings, and the platform strips follow local grades and maintain rail clearance.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X follows the limestone facade east-southeast. Positive Z faces Place du 11-Novembre-1918 and Rue du 8 Mai 1945. Negative Z follows the outgoing tracks.",
  "limitations": [
    "The main terminal footprint, its signed axis and the track pairs follow Protomaps PMTiles. The model uses the standard 52 m sea-level terrain datum. Most exterior heights and the long shelter terminations are photo estimates.",
    "The fourteen platform islands and their roofs follow sampled terrain and mapped rail spacing. The two seated city figures, clock reliefs and platform fittings are modeled at viewing scale. Interior rooms and temporary station works are outside the exterior scope."
  ],
